+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for helping! Every contribution counts: bug reports, testing on your OS, docs,
+UI polish, and new engine adapters.
+
+## Ways to help
+
+- 🪟 **Test on Windows or macOS** and report what happens (these platforms need testers most).
+- 🐛 **Report bugs** with the issue template, including your OS, CPU/RAM and the relevant
+  lines from `logs/api.log` / `logs/worker.log` (they never contain your script text).
+- 🗣️ **Listen and review** audio quality with `scripts/evaluate.py` (especially Urdu and Hindi speakers).
+- 🧩 **Add an engine adapter** (see docs/MODEL_SETUP.md → "Adding another engine").
+- 🎨 **Improve the UI** and accessibility.
+
+## Development setup
+
+```bash
+scripts/setup.sh            # or scripts\setup.ps1 on Windows
+scripts/dev.sh              # backend :8765 + Vite hot reload :5173
+```
+
+## Before opening a pull request
+
+```bash
+cd backend && ../.venv/bin/ruff check app tests && ../.venv/bin/mypy app && ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest
+cd frontend && npx tsc -b && npx vitest run
+```
+
+If you have Kokoro installed, also run the real-inference and E2E tests (docs/TESTING.md).
+
+## Ground rules
+
+- Keep it **local-first**: no telemetry, and no silent network calls.
+- **Don't overclaim.** A language or engine is "verified" only after real tests.
+- Model weights must have a clear licence; record code and weight licences separately in `registry.json`.
+- Schema changes need an Alembic migration.
+- Keep PRs focused, and add tests for behaviour changes.
+
+By contributing you agree your code is released under the MIT licence.
